# The oracle images, pinned.
#
# One line per oracle, tab-separated: <name> <image-ref> <version> <what it
# answers>.
#
# Two kinds of pin and they are not the same guarantee. A stock image is pinned by digest and
# the digest is the whole guarantee. An image **built here** cannot be: two
# builds of one Containerfile are not two copies of one image. What is pinned
# instead is everything the build reads - the base by digest, pip packages by
# exact version, Debian's font packages by full apt version - and the run-time
# version check is the real guarantee, which is why oracle_env.check_pin() runs
# in *both* modes in this library. `unicode` relaxed that check in host mode
# because every image it names is a stock one; here there is no stock image to
# name, so the relaxation would leave nothing checking anything.
#
# The version field is what the reference must say it is when asked. Raising a
# pin is deliberate: a new fontTools is new answers, and a new answer that
# disagrees is a finding to triage rather than a regression to fix.
#
# Building it:
#   podman build -t ghoti-font-oracle-fonttools:4.66.0 \
#       -f tools/oracle/containers/fonttools/Containerfile \
#       tools/oracle/containers/fonttools
# `make oracle-build` does exactly that.

# fontTools, and the real fonts. Both halves are deliberate: this is the
# reference for every table's fields (ttx_diff) and for every codepoint's glyph
# (cmap_diff), *and* the image the fixture generator will run in, so that a
# fixture's bytes depend on a pinned fontTools rather than on whatever the host
# has (design.md section 14.7).
fonttools	localhost/ghoti-font-oracle-fonttools:4.66.0	fontTools 4.66.0 Pillow 12.3.0	Every sfnt table's fields, every cmap's mapping, EBLC/EBDT strikes glyph by glyph, PCF and BDF bitmaps through Pillow, and the corpus of real fonts - including the whole Debian population of embedded bitmap strikes, which is two fonts

# Not here yet, and each is a phase rather than an afternoon:
#   freetype   outline and coverage differentials (phase 1), built here,
#              driver compiled inside the image against FreeType alone
#   harfbuzz   hb-shape, already a batch tool (phase 3)
#   pango      pango-view, for paragraph layout (phase 3b)
#   xfonts     bdftopcf and psftools: a *second* reading of PCF, and the only
#              reading of PSF and `.hex` there is. Pillow covers PCF's bitmaps
#              and BDF outright, so what is still missing is PSF, `.hex`, and an
#              independent reading of PCF's encodings table - see bitmap_diff.py
#
# `freetype` has one more job than the list above gives it: it is the only reader
# of `EBDT` outside fontTools, and fontTools cannot parse `mona.ttf`'s `EBLC` at
# all. So that font's three strikes are read here and nowhere else, which
# eblc_diff.py prints beside its skip. If the freetype image ever lands,
# `mona.ttf` is the first thing to point it at.
